If you mean new relationship energy, give your wife a chance to meet a version of you she rarely gets to see lately, and give yourself a chance to meet hers. You already know each other as parents and partners running a household. There’s still plenty you can surprise each other with.

* Bring back the buildup. Text her on a Tuesday: “I miss flirting with you. I’m taking you out Friday if you’re up for it. I’ll handle the kids.” Then flirt a little between Tuesday and Friday.
* Change what you do together. Take her dancing if that sounds fun to both of you. Or each pick one stop for a night out and keep yours a surprise. Give yourselves something to react to together besides the day’s logistics.
* Get curious about who she is now. Try “What would you do with a whole Saturday to yourself these days?” Follow the answer that surprises you.
* Say what you actually notice. “You had this look on your face when you were telling that story. I wanted to kiss you.” A specific moment tells her you’re paying attention.

And use your costume insight. Dress like you’re going on a date with her. Put on the jacket you feel good in. Meet her at the bar if you can. There’s something about looking up and seeing the person you live with walk into a room to meet you.